        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "aa67bc22-647b-32bb-a342-693d943da931",
                "word": "théoriquement",
                "pos": "adv",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "75064081-914a-3cb1-9d31-51e0b67d133c",
                        "entry_id": "aa67bc22-647b-32bb-a342-693d943da931",
                        "glosses": [
                            "D’une manière théorique."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d55f25b8-cf96-41a9-94f9-90f7012611be",
                                "sense_id": "75064081-914a-3cb1-9d31-51e0b67d133c",
                                "text": "Lorsque Newton entreprit de calculer théoriquement les réfractions produites par l'atmosphère, il donna à celle-ci une constitution qui suppose implicitement la température constante à toutes les hauteurs; […]."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3cfdf8cc-0999-3214-b341-2e5afe8aa21f",
                        "entry_id": "aa67bc22-647b-32bb-a342-693d943da931",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A priori."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "familiar"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1a804f45-2cdc-4158-98c2-eada1cccb3fe",
                                "sense_id": "3cfdf8cc-0999-3214-b341-2e5afe8aa21f",
                                "text": "Le Président a qualifié d’« hypothétique » la possibilité de démilitariser Quemoy et Matsu en échange d'un cessez-le-feu, néanmoins il a reconnu que c'était théoriquement envisagé par la diplomatie américaine."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d644e077-4064-4fb6-b837-008d9b90d86f",
                                "sense_id": "3cfdf8cc-0999-3214-b341-2e5afe8aa21f",
                                "text": "Si la pêche du sandre est théoriquement possible toute l'année, les deux meilleures périodes semblent être la fin du printemps, juste après le frai, puis l'automne."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "79a09996-eeba-4f1e-9585-b68bbcd0e517",
                                "sense_id": "3cfdf8cc-0999-3214-b341-2e5afe8aa21f",
                                "text": "Toute caravane qui entrait dans le territoire du sultan d'Ayar devait payer cette taxe, moyennant quoi elle était, théoriquement du moins, sous la protection du sultan jusqu'à ce qu'elle quitte le territoire placé sous son commandement."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "0f0f3943-81fb-3af2-b717-689cfcd25972",
                        "entry_id": "aa67bc22-647b-32bb-a342-693d943da931",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Comme l'on devrait y parvenir selon la théorie."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "ironic"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "3a1107d9-18c8-4dbd-a494-b5f6cc31ba36",
                                "sense_id": "0f0f3943-81fb-3af2-b717-689cfcd25972",
                                "text": "Je comprends alors que ces dix images doivent « théoriquement » se réunir en une seule pour constituer une vue panoramique. Malheureusement il n'en est rien ; aucune n'est à la même hauteur que sa voisine, ça danse terriblement."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fdca7d00-b032-4508-923a-9ae8cc7dd91e",
                        "source_entry_id": "aa67bc22-647b-32bb-a342-693d943da931",
                        "target_lang_word": "in theory",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "in theory",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "72d34862-f7ac-35f5-bffb-cb7de5c88320",
                                        "entry_id": "a4ca124e-5c7e-3985-9de9-a433bfcf8004",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Theoretically."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1f02d9e9-f1a8-4ea4-b39f-896c4b91fc66",
                                                "sense_id": "72d34862-f7ac-35f5-bffb-cb7de5c88320",
                                                "text": "That sounds fine in theory, but will it work in practice?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d164e4e7-3b91-40af-b25f-5fc62995de55",
                        "source_entry_id": "aa67bc22-647b-32bb-a342-693d943da931",
                        "target_lang_word": "theoretically",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "theoretically",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c4fc21c9-a342-35f5-912b-f4f8ed8d6ff1",
                                        "entry_id": "7272a7be-dba0-3136-a1dc-d6e2faa99ccc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "in theory; on paper"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f47ad9cb-a6c6-457d-a0b1-cb43fe4d6418",
                                                "sense_id": "c4fc21c9-a342-35f5-912b-f4f8ed8d6ff1",
                                                "text": "I haven't tested it, but theoretically it ought to fly."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "53b40cd8-2b1c-42b9-8450-e06203cd8d3f",
                                                "sense_id": "c4fc21c9-a342-35f5-912b-f4f8ed8d6ff1",
                                                "text": "Of course, it will never get -100 here like it does in Antarctica, but a 300-degree swing was still theoretically possible on a record-cold Minnesota morning–if we got the sauna hot enough."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c4caea21-4987-371d-8a51-471829d0d9db",
                                        "entry_id": "7272a7be-dba0-3136-a1dc-d6e2faa99ccc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "in a theoretical manner"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6463050a-9112-48a2-a33a-07bab1a28e96",
                                                "sense_id": "c4caea21-4987-371d-8a51-471829d0d9db",
                                                "text": "I solved the problem theoretically rather than practically."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "9c7baf72-889c-3626-8e36-3c2a083d471d",
                                        "entry_id": "7272a7be-dba0-3136-a1dc-d6e2faa99ccc",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "in theory though not necessarily in reality."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2558aa5e-18cd-4c9c-b124-1bee4c910995",
                                                "sense_id": "9c7baf72-889c-3626-8e36-3c2a083d471d",
                                                "text": "Rumors of an indictment had spread through this heavily gay and lesbian community since shortly after the theoretically secret investigation began in 1984."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1d4ffd7e-2fdf-4ad2-afcb-fd98fac75276",
                                                "sense_id": "9c7baf72-889c-3626-8e36-3c2a083d471d",
                                                "text": "No, but insurance does cover it. Theoretically."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3e2c711b-d3b7-4664-a9b7-9a9833d6d28a",
                        "source_entry_id": "aa67bc22-647b-32bb-a342-693d943da931",
